Narrator: As the Ichthyos and Krakenfolk begin to run out of options, a call from south of the waters draws their attention.
Narrator: It’s… a boat?
Noelle: We’re back! #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Saorise: Well, would you look at that. #portrait:Saorise
Amelia: Okay, this thing is <i>definitely</i> gonna split in half! #portrait:AmeliaSilly
Narrator: You finally make it to shore, explaining that your ship should be able to act as a ‘prop’ of sorts, so that the rock can be moved up slightly.
Noelle: Then those who are trapped can be rescued. Is that alright? #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Narrator: An Ichthyos lady with an elegant aura smiles.
Saorise: Come on everyone! You heard the girl! #portrait:Saorise
Narrator: With a bit of a struggle, the rock finally budges! Two girls swim out, thankfully uninjured save for a few scratches and cuts.
Narrator: The boat, however…
Zale: You two, thanks so much for the help! #portrait:Zale
Zale: Is your boat…? #portrait:Zale
Noelle: …I think… we can just leave it there. #portrait:NoelleSad 
Noelle: I’ll see if it’s fixable after everyone’s less stressed. #portrait:NoelleUm
